{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
AN OLD DRAGON'S WRATH

26
00:01:36,732 --> 00:01:37,817
[mysterious music playing]

27
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,069
- [female panther] Hey, young man.
- [Legoshi] Hmm?

28
00:01:40,152 --> 00:01:43,739
{\an8}How would you like to try a special
energy drink, just for carnivores?

29
00:01:43,823 --> 00:01:47,034
{\an8}Uh, I'm okay. I have more stamina
than you would think.

30
00:01:47,118 --> 00:01:50,830
{\an8}Nah, come on, just trust me.
You'll love it. You can try one.

31
00:01:50,913 --> 00:01:52,581
{\an8}It won't hurt. Here.

32
00:01:53,207 --> 00:01:54,291
{\an8}[fizzes]

33
00:01:54,375 --> 00:01:57,586
Oh. No, no. I should probably go...

34
00:01:58,129 --> 00:01:59,421
I... [sniffs]

35
00:02:00,047 --> 00:02:00,881
Huh?

36
00:02:01,757 --> 00:02:03,509
[sniffs, moans]

37
00:02:03,592 --> 00:02:07,012
[male panther chuckles]
<i>We'll have this kid hooked in no time.</i>

38
00:02:07,096 --> 00:02:10,182
[groaning]

39
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:16,272
[inhaling]

40
00:02:16,814 --> 00:02:18,732
- [sneezes]
- [both exclaim in disgust]

41
00:02:18,816 --> 00:02:21,944
- [coughs] Sorry, it was cold last night.
- [female panther] Are you kidding?

42
00:02:22,027 --> 00:02:24,113
And I slept in only my underwear, so, uh...

43
00:02:24,905 --> 00:02:26,031
Yeah.

44
00:02:26,115 --> 00:02:29,118
Yeah, anyway, that energy drink of yours,

45
00:02:29,201 --> 00:02:32,580
it contains herbivore blood
and bone tissue, I believe.

46
00:02:32,663 --> 00:02:33,914
[male black panther] Uh...

47
00:02:33,998 --> 00:02:35,624
Sorry, not interested.

48
00:02:36,417 --> 00:02:37,251
Well, see ya.

49
00:02:38,836 --> 00:02:41,130
- Whoa, wait.
- [lizard] What's up with him?

50
00:02:42,298 --> 00:02:43,549
[Legoshi] <i>Just let it go.</i>

51
00:02:44,341 --> 00:02:46,260
<i>It's for the best
that you don't get involved.</i>

52
00:02:46,343 --> 00:02:49,722
[inhales heavily] <i>This kind of thing
happens all the time in the real world.</i>

53
00:02:49,805 --> 00:02:52,016
[Louis] Is that really
how you feel, Legoshi?

54
00:02:52,099 --> 00:02:53,100
[Legoshi] Hmm?

55
00:02:54,101 --> 00:02:57,855
[Louis] You went so far as to eat my leg
for the sake of justice,

56
00:02:57,938 --> 00:03:02,109
yet you're going to let them get away
with trying to hustle someone like that?

57
00:03:02,693 --> 00:03:03,694
[gasps softly]

58
00:03:03,777 --> 00:03:06,113
It's time to get angry, Legoshi.

59
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:11,535
[Legoshi] <i>If you think it'll help, Louis.</i>

60
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:16,206
Uh... What's your deal, man?

61
00:03:16,290 --> 00:03:20,252
[Legoshi] Well,
I ate my friend while he was still alive.

62
00:03:21,545 --> 00:03:24,131
I only react to the flesh
of living herbivores,

63
00:03:25,049 --> 00:03:28,719
but I want, more than anything,
to get along with those living herbivores.

64
00:03:28,802 --> 00:03:30,846
You keep wagging that tongue
and I'll cut it out!

65
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:34,308
Have you ever, even once,
thought about the lives of the herbivores

66
00:03:34,391 --> 00:03:36,477
that end up in that drink you're selling?

67
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,811
Or do they mean nothing to you?

68
00:03:37,895 --> 00:03:39,271
Huh?

69
00:03:39,355 --> 00:03:43,150
What are you, a softie? You really need
to embrace your nature, kid.

70
00:03:43,234 --> 00:03:44,902
- [growls]
- [grunts]

71
00:03:44,985 --> 00:03:47,696
[both grunting]

72
00:03:49,198 --> 00:03:50,532
[exhales]

73
00:03:50,616 --> 00:03:52,284
[Legoshi] <i>"Embrace your nature"?</i>

74
00:03:53,452 --> 00:03:55,329
<i>"Embrace your nature."</i>

75
00:03:55,412 --> 00:03:57,289
[heart beating, laughing]

76
00:03:57,373 --> 00:03:59,708
[male panther] What are you
laughing about, you freak?

77
00:03:59,792 --> 00:04:01,502
[grunts]

78
00:04:01,585 --> 00:04:03,337
[groans]

79
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:04,463
- [gasps]
- Huh.

80
00:04:04,546 --> 00:04:09,301
[Legoshi] <i>Oh, I'll embrace my nature
for the sake of the herbivores.</i>

81
00:04:10,177 --> 00:04:12,179
- [growls]
- [gasps]

82
00:04:12,263 --> 00:04:14,306
[yelling]

83
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:16,392
[both grunting]

84
00:04:23,232 --> 00:04:25,109
[panther yells, grunts]

85
00:04:25,192 --> 00:04:27,194
[both grunting]

86
00:04:27,278 --> 00:04:28,946
[groaning]

87
00:04:29,029 --> 00:04:30,948
[both grunting]

88
00:04:31,991 --> 00:04:33,325
[groans]

89
00:04:33,409 --> 00:04:34,952
- [Legoshi grunting]
- [groaning]

90
00:04:35,035 --> 00:04:37,037
[both grunting]

91
00:04:38,205 --> 00:04:42,167
[Legoshi] <i>My fangs are bared.
My heart is going to beat out of my chest.</i>

92
00:04:42,251 --> 00:04:46,255
- [growling]
- I quit, I give up. We won't sell it!

93
00:04:46,338 --> 00:04:49,174
- [groans, whimpers]
- [Legoshi] I can't hear you.

94
00:04:50,634 --> 00:04:53,012
[choking]

95
00:04:53,595 --> 00:04:57,516
[Legoshi] <i>For the sake of the herbivores,
I have to destroy him.</i>

96
00:04:59,059 --> 00:05:00,728
- [grunts]
- [female panther gasps]

97
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,771
[female panther] Stop already!

98
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:09,445
[Legoshi] <i>My whole body is screaming,
"Go ahead, embrace your true nature!"</i>

99
00:05:10,154 --> 00:05:12,406
- [whimpering]
- [Legoshi] Hmm.

100
00:05:13,324 --> 00:05:15,242
- [grunting]
- [male panther groaning]

101
00:05:15,326 --> 00:05:17,328
[siren approaching]

102
00:05:19,705 --> 00:05:20,748
Huh?

103
00:05:20,831 --> 00:05:22,458
[female panther] Let's get out of here!

104
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,961
[officer] Hey, stop right there! Hey!

105
00:05:26,962 --> 00:05:29,089
You there! Hey, wait!

106
00:05:32,593 --> 00:05:35,429
SHISHI-GUMI

107
00:05:35,512 --> 00:05:37,014
[Free] Hey, why do you think

108
00:05:37,097 --> 00:05:40,392
they stuck you and me out here
to collect the revenue, huh?

109
00:05:41,018 --> 00:05:43,562
Not like I care. Think about it like this.

110
00:05:43,645 --> 00:05:46,732
We get to get out from under
that creepy new boss for a while.

111
00:05:46,815 --> 00:05:49,443
- [lizard panting]
- Hey! Right here.

112
00:05:50,194 --> 00:05:52,571
[lizard panting]

113
00:05:52,654 --> 00:05:55,449
You assholes, how long did you plan
to keep us waiting?

114
00:05:55,532 --> 00:05:56,658
That's everything.

115
00:05:58,452 --> 00:06:00,496
That's all you got in one day?

116
00:06:00,579 --> 00:06:03,082
Who cares, man?
This isn't what they said it was.

117
00:06:03,165 --> 00:06:04,291
What what was?

118
00:06:04,374 --> 00:06:06,627
Kines, the energy drink.

119
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:09,755
You said just a whiff
and they'd all come running, right?

120
00:06:09,838 --> 00:06:12,466
We had this wolf kid, he just walked away.

121
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:14,093
[both] Huh.

122
00:06:14,176 --> 00:06:17,596
- What kind of carnivore...
- Yeah, that's a little strange.

123
00:06:17,679 --> 00:06:18,847
Want to hear "strange"?

124
00:06:18,931 --> 00:06:23,060
He came back and started ranting about
payback for the sacrificed herbivores

125
00:06:23,143 --> 00:06:25,187
and went on a total rampage.

126
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:28,232
[lizard] <i>Damn him. He'll pay for that.</i>

127
00:06:28,315 --> 00:06:31,610
What do you think?
Should we go back and let the boss know?

128
00:06:31,693 --> 00:06:32,861
[Free] Hmm.

129
00:06:32,945 --> 00:06:34,279
[gasps] Hey!

130
00:06:34,363 --> 00:06:36,782
- [lizard] Sorry, tell them I tried!
- [both] Huh?

131
00:06:42,204 --> 00:06:44,206
[serene music playing]

132
00:06:48,210 --> 00:06:49,878
[Bill] Okay, listen up.

133
00:06:49,962 --> 00:06:53,757
In light of the separate education
for herbivores and carnivores,

134
00:06:53,841 --> 00:06:56,468
mixed club activities like ours
have been banned.

135
00:06:57,010 --> 00:06:58,220
Anyway, we're here today

136
00:06:58,303 --> 00:07:02,015
so that we can discuss and decide
on the future of the drama club together.

137
00:07:02,099 --> 00:07:04,184
- Anybody got a question?
- [Kai] Yeah.

138
00:07:04,268 --> 00:07:06,979
Why are you acting like
you're the real president around here?

139
00:07:07,062 --> 00:07:09,440
- What's the deal, dude?
- Doesn't suit you.

140
00:07:09,523 --> 00:07:10,941
[Bill groans] Shut up, would ya?

141
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:12,359
He's right. Be respectful.

142
00:07:12,443 --> 00:07:13,986
HAVE SEPARATE CLUBS
OR SUSPEND THE CLUB

143
00:07:14,069 --> 00:07:17,656
Bill is our legitimate president.
Louis chose him to run the club.

144
00:07:17,739 --> 00:07:21,994
[Kai] Uh, okay, then in that case,
I vote to cease club activities for now.

145
00:07:22,077 --> 00:07:22,911
Huh?

146
00:07:22,995 --> 00:07:26,999
Louis, who stood up to a devourer alone,
appointed you, a carnivore.

147
00:07:27,082 --> 00:07:29,835
He could've chosen anyone. But it was you.

148
00:07:29,918 --> 00:07:32,963
In that case,
why cave and divide the club into two

149
00:07:33,046 --> 00:07:36,091
when, instead, we could protest
the whole school?

150
00:07:36,175 --> 00:07:38,093
When'd you get so smart?

151
00:07:38,177 --> 00:07:42,556
But if we do that, we may never
be able to do club activities again.

152
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:44,766
[sighs] Good point.

153
00:07:44,850 --> 00:07:48,395
What are you saying? We've always
done well in here as a mixed group.

154
00:07:48,479 --> 00:07:51,148
We can use that
to persuade the school. Duh.

155
00:07:51,648 --> 00:07:52,816
Always done well?

156
00:07:53,525 --> 00:07:55,110
- Do you think that's true?
- Huh?

157
00:07:55,861 --> 00:08:00,532
I'm sorry to say it, but there were two
major incidents in here last year alone.

158
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:04,203
I'm not convinced that
that counts as us "doing well."

159
00:08:04,745 --> 00:08:07,706
- That's a little out of line.
- No, it's not. It's the truth.

160
00:08:08,457 --> 00:08:11,084
Our club is the whole reason
they're splitting us up.

161
00:08:11,168 --> 00:08:13,170
They can't risk us getting hurt again.

162
00:08:13,253 --> 00:08:16,423
[Fudge] Oh, I get it. You're saying
carnivores are to blame for everything.

163
00:08:16,507 --> 00:08:18,425
[Ellen] What? That's not what I said.

164
00:08:18,509 --> 00:08:20,594
Okay, let's just chill out.

165
00:08:21,637 --> 00:08:22,846
[both sigh]

166
00:08:23,555 --> 00:08:25,015
What do you think, Juno?

167
00:08:27,559 --> 00:08:28,810
Coexistence.

168
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:31,980
All of us working together.

169
00:08:33,732 --> 00:08:35,817
I think the most important thing

170
00:08:35,901 --> 00:08:40,197
is that we do not allow the principles
of existing together to die out now.

171
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,658
[sighs]

172
00:08:43,367 --> 00:08:47,955
If you take a look around, you'll see that
our club was founded on those principles.

173
00:08:48,038 --> 00:08:51,750
For us to create art and harmony.
That was the spirit.

174
00:08:52,376 --> 00:08:57,256
And if we share in that spirit,
we're still one club, even if we're apart.

175
00:08:57,339 --> 00:09:00,759
And you may not agree,
but I think it's important to try.

176
00:09:01,301 --> 00:09:06,598
Keep the fire, even if that means
we do have to separate for a little while.

177
00:09:06,682 --> 00:09:08,267
She's got a point.

178
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:09,518
That's Juno for you.

179
00:09:09,601 --> 00:09:12,563
[Pina] If that's the tactic
we're going with, then I'm out.

180
00:09:12,646 --> 00:09:14,856
- [all] Huh?
- What, did I stutter?

181
00:09:15,607 --> 00:09:19,444
It's been a good six months,
but it's time to move on.

182
00:09:20,654 --> 00:09:23,240
See, I'm not into the whole
long-distance thing.

183
00:09:24,241 --> 00:09:28,203
"Absence makes the heart grow fonder."
I mean, has that ever worked out?

184
00:09:29,454 --> 00:09:30,747
And you know what?

185
00:09:30,831 --> 00:09:34,876
This club and meeting you carnivores
has taught me something about myself.

186
00:09:36,211 --> 00:09:38,797
All that power you have is so enticing.

187
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:43,135
Those sharp claws and fangs of yours
make me all tingly.

188
00:09:43,218 --> 00:09:46,096
[shudders] I can't get enough of it.

189
00:09:46,179 --> 00:09:50,601
Alas, if we're going to split up,
there's no point in me staying.

190
00:09:51,476 --> 00:09:52,311
So I'm out.

191
00:09:53,061 --> 00:09:54,479
[all sigh, exclaim]

192
00:09:54,563 --> 00:09:56,732
Bye. Take care. See you around.

193
00:10:00,193 --> 00:10:01,028
[door opens]

194
00:10:02,904 --> 00:10:04,531
- You don't need to say it.
- [door closes]

195
00:10:04,615 --> 00:10:05,490
What?

196
00:10:05,574 --> 00:10:09,119
"If only Louis were still here with us."
You were thinking it.

197
00:10:10,162 --> 00:10:12,414
[sighs] You're right.

198
00:10:12,497 --> 00:10:15,500
[metal creaking]

199
00:10:31,183 --> 00:10:32,100
[grunts softly]

200
00:10:33,852 --> 00:10:34,770
What the...

201
00:10:36,855 --> 00:10:39,149
[gasps softly] Legoshi.

202
00:10:40,025 --> 00:10:41,443
[gasps] Oh, hey, Haru!

203
00:10:41,526 --> 00:10:43,278
[Haru chuckles]

204
00:10:45,489 --> 00:10:47,407
- What's going on?
- [Legoshi chuckles]

205
00:10:47,491 --> 00:10:48,784
[both chuckle]

206
00:10:48,867 --> 00:10:50,535
Huh? What is it?

207
00:10:50,619 --> 00:10:52,996
- [chuckles] You look so cute.
- [giggles]

208
00:10:53,622 --> 00:10:55,707
Come on, is that the best you can do?

209
00:10:55,791 --> 00:10:57,250
[both chuckle]

210
00:10:57,334 --> 00:11:00,295
Are you off of work today?
We didn't talk about hanging out.

211
00:11:00,379 --> 00:11:02,839
- Mmm, yeah, that's true.
- Huh?

212
00:11:03,423 --> 00:11:05,384
- [sighs softly]
- It's okay, I won't ask.

213
00:11:06,051 --> 00:11:08,553
And I can see
you're already healing up anyway, so...

214
00:11:08,637 --> 00:11:12,182
Uh, oh, this? It's nothing.
[chuckles nervously] I just hit my face.

215
00:11:12,265 --> 00:11:14,684
- Uh... Hmm?
- Never mind that.

216
00:11:14,768 --> 00:11:18,730
Listen, I came here 'cause there's
something I've been meaning to tell you.

217
00:11:19,606 --> 00:11:21,733
Because I want to be honest
with you, Haru.

218
00:11:22,526 --> 00:11:23,652
Hmm?

219
00:11:23,735 --> 00:11:24,820
The thing is...

220
00:11:25,445 --> 00:11:26,363
Mmm-hmm?

221
00:11:26,446 --> 00:11:28,949
Well, I, uh... I...

222
00:11:30,033 --> 00:11:30,909
[bus stops]

223
00:11:30,992 --> 00:11:33,203
There's something
I've been meaning to tell you.

224
00:11:33,286 --> 00:11:35,205
- You said that.
- Oh, yeah.

225
00:11:35,288 --> 00:11:36,706
- Well...
- [Haru's father] Haru!

226
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:38,166
- [Haru gasps]
- Huh?

227
00:11:38,250 --> 00:11:40,419
- Watch yourself, wolf!
- [gasps nervously]

228
00:11:40,502 --> 00:11:42,629
Thank you so much
for picking up my change, sir!

229
00:11:42,712 --> 00:11:44,840
- You're a lifesaver! Bye!
- Uh... Huh?

230
00:11:44,923 --> 00:11:46,633
- [pants]
- Wait.

231
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:50,554
[Haru] You're early today. Hi, Dad.

232
00:11:50,637 --> 00:11:52,055
[gasps] <i>That's her dad?</i>

233
00:11:52,722 --> 00:11:55,725
Yeah. Have you still not gotten
a bus pass?

234
00:11:55,809 --> 00:11:57,561
Uh, there was kind of a mix-up,

235
00:11:57,644 --> 00:12:00,772
so my student ID is coming
a bit later than I thought.

236
00:12:00,856 --> 00:12:03,608
- [Haru's father] That's unfortunate...
<i>- I didn't even get to say hello.</i>

237
00:12:04,443 --> 00:12:06,027
<i>I guess being a carnivore means</i>

238
00:12:06,111 --> 00:12:09,573
{\an8}<i>some things are just going to be
more... difficult.</i>

239
00:12:09,656 --> 00:12:12,576
{\an8}- [Haru] And you know you don't need to.
- [Haru's father] Is that so?

240
00:12:18,665 --> 00:12:21,668
{\an8}MAI MAI MILK

241
00:12:25,714 --> 00:12:27,716
[choking, whimpering]

242
00:12:29,384 --> 00:12:31,720
Listen up, and remember this.

243
00:12:32,387 --> 00:12:35,056
The reason our society functions at all

244
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:38,101
is because we herbivores
have been extremely tolerant.

245
00:12:39,561 --> 00:12:42,481
[grunts, groans]

246
00:12:43,732 --> 00:12:46,485
I'm here for when the goodwill runs out.

247
00:12:46,568 --> 00:12:50,780
[spluttering] I'm so sorry. Please.
I'll send them home by 8. [whimpers]

248
00:12:51,364 --> 00:12:52,616
You've been warned.

249
00:12:52,699 --> 00:12:55,327
- [snow leopard whimpers] Understood.
- [cows speaking indistinctly]

250
00:12:55,410 --> 00:12:57,746
You've been suffering under him
for too long.

251
00:12:57,829 --> 00:13:01,291
I should've been here much sooner.
Please forgive me.

252
00:13:03,043 --> 00:13:05,545
- [cow 1] Thank you, thank you again.
- [cow 2] So glad you came.

253
00:13:10,509 --> 00:13:11,551
[Corne] Mr. Yahya.

254
00:13:12,511 --> 00:13:14,221
[Yahya] What did you find out?

255
00:13:14,304 --> 00:13:17,974
[Corne] Well, the gray wolf
who got into that big brawl

256
00:13:18,058 --> 00:13:19,893
with the Kines dealers in the alley?

257
00:13:21,186 --> 00:13:24,314
He is for sure the same young beast
you read about.

258
00:13:24,397 --> 00:13:27,776
You know, the one who ate
his friend's leg in January?

259
00:13:27,859 --> 00:13:31,947
Yes, I kind of had a feeling.
There's something about this guy.

260
00:13:32,489 --> 00:13:35,367
Yeah, like, does he think
he's a vigilante or something?

261
00:13:35,450 --> 00:13:39,746
Not like we need one. Beastar like you
has got the city covered, Mr. Yahya.

262
00:13:39,829 --> 00:13:42,707
That may be, but there's a limit
to what one old horse can do

263
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,918
when it comes down to protecting the city.

264
00:13:45,001 --> 00:13:46,294
[Corne] Now, hold on.

265
00:13:46,378 --> 00:13:49,089
Don't get me wrong, I'm glad for the help.

266
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:52,884
Because if I can't rid the streets
of that energy drink,

267
00:13:52,968 --> 00:13:56,846
the public safety I've been working
all these years for is still way off.

268
00:13:58,598 --> 00:14:02,852
[Yahya] <i>A horse's field of vision is ever
so slightly short of absolute panoramic.</i>

269
00:14:03,812 --> 00:14:05,855
<i>350 degrees to be exact.</i>

270
00:14:06,773 --> 00:14:09,818
<i>If I could make up for
that ten-degree blind spot,</i>

271
00:14:09,901 --> 00:14:13,446
<i>the dregs of society
would have nowhere left to hide.</i>

272
00:14:14,865 --> 00:14:18,201
<i>The criminals that operate in the shadows
are taunting me.</i>

273
00:14:19,494 --> 00:14:23,748
<i>If I had the 360-degree field of vision
like I used to when you were here,</i>

274
00:14:25,125 --> 00:14:27,878
<i>I'd be able to annihilate them
once and for all.</i>

275
00:14:29,254 --> 00:14:31,089
<i>My gentle monster...</i>

276
00:14:32,173 --> 00:14:34,634
[inhales heavily] <i>you ruined it all.</i>

277
00:14:36,511 --> 00:14:41,224
<i>The idea of a perfect fighting force,
the perfect society,</i>

278
00:14:41,308 --> 00:14:44,561
<i>building perfect trust, gone forever.</i>

279
00:14:45,645 --> 00:14:50,066
<i>It may be only ten degrees,
but it's still ten degrees from perfect,</i>

280
00:14:50,734 --> 00:14:51,651
<i>Gosha.</i>

281
00:15:15,842 --> 00:15:16,801
[sighs]

282
00:15:17,636 --> 00:15:20,221
<i>I feel like every time I take
a step closer to Haru,</i>

283
00:15:20,305 --> 00:15:22,641
<i>I wind up taking another step back.</i>

284
00:15:23,308 --> 00:15:27,020
[sighs] <i>It's not fair that
maintaining a bond with another species</i>

285
00:15:27,103 --> 00:15:29,230
<i>has to be so complicated.</i>

286
00:15:31,566 --> 00:15:32,400
Hmm?

287
00:15:35,028 --> 00:15:36,571
[mysterious music playing]

288
00:15:36,655 --> 00:15:39,491
<i>A lizard. Revenge for yesterday?</i>

289
00:15:50,251 --> 00:15:52,253
[sizzling]

290
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:02,764
[Legoshi] Hmm?

291
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:04,849
Hmm.

292
00:16:06,643 --> 00:16:07,602
[gasps softly]

293
00:16:11,606 --> 00:16:13,900
[gasps, gulps]

294
00:16:14,693 --> 00:16:16,945
[Legoshi groans softly]

295
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,116
[gulps]

296
00:16:21,199 --> 00:16:25,328
<i>A Komodo dragon's venom
doesn't affect its own kind.</i>

297
00:16:25,412 --> 00:16:26,246
Hmm.

298
00:16:26,329 --> 00:16:30,083
- Legoshi! How the hell are ya?
- [Legoshi chuckles]

299
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:32,919
Hi, Grandpa. How about
a normal greeting next time?

300
00:16:33,503 --> 00:16:37,173
Surely, you don't mind
a bit of your old granddad's venom?

301
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:40,510
You're my only grandchild.
Who else am I supposed to mess with?

302
00:16:41,177 --> 00:16:42,137
I know.

303
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:44,055
[quirky music playing]

304
00:16:44,139 --> 00:16:47,392
[Legoshi] <i>That venom that can bring death
to many other creatures,</i>

305
00:16:47,475 --> 00:16:52,272
<i>but, to me, it's always tasted like
a bittersweet marmalade.</i>

306
00:16:54,357 --> 00:16:57,110
[Gosha] <i>Hey, you still like french fries,
don't ya?</i>

307
00:16:57,944 --> 00:17:00,321
Huh? Oh, uh, yeah, sure.

308
00:17:00,405 --> 00:17:03,783
- All right then, let's go eat some.
- Uh... now?

309
00:17:03,867 --> 00:17:05,076
Yeah, now!

310
00:17:06,995 --> 00:17:09,956
{\an8}[Legoshi] <i>I liked them a lot more
when I was a child</i>

311
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,542
{\an8}<i>I mean, it's not like
they're anything special now.</i>

312
00:17:13,334 --> 00:17:16,504
[Gosha laughs] So this is chilly for you?

313
00:17:17,714 --> 00:17:18,631
[Legoshi] Kind of.

314
00:17:18,715 --> 00:17:19,549
<i>It's fine.</i>

315
00:17:20,717 --> 00:17:22,677
<i>We don't have to talk about anything.</i>

316
00:17:22,761 --> 00:17:24,095
[music ends]

317
00:17:24,929 --> 00:17:27,307
- Why don't we just sit by the door?
- Hmm?

318
00:17:27,390 --> 00:17:28,558
Not busy in here.

319
00:17:29,434 --> 00:17:31,728
We don't have to head
straight for the back. Come on.

320
00:17:31,811 --> 00:17:34,230
[hesitates] No, but I...

321
00:17:34,773 --> 00:17:39,194
<i>Legoshi, don't tell me
you've already forgotten the rule.</i>

322
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:44,365
<i>In a restaurant, we always choose a table
somewhere in the back.</i>

323
00:17:44,449 --> 00:17:45,909
<i>Don't want to cause trouble.</i>

324
00:17:46,701 --> 00:17:51,122
<i>A venomous Komodo dragon like me
tends to bring out the worst in people.</i>

325
00:17:51,831 --> 00:17:53,249
<i>Best not to tempt fate.</i>

326
00:17:54,375 --> 00:17:56,002
<i>It's just how it is.</i>

327
00:17:56,628 --> 00:17:58,463
[Legoshi] I've always found it
kind of weird.

328
00:17:59,714 --> 00:18:01,758
You shouldn't have to sit in the back.

329
00:18:01,841 --> 00:18:04,260
I mean, it's not like
you've done anything wrong.

330
00:18:04,344 --> 00:18:06,304
[groans softly]

331
00:18:06,387 --> 00:18:08,473
- [owner] It's fine, sit down.
- [both] Huh?

332
00:18:10,767 --> 00:18:11,851
[Gosha grunts softly]

333
00:18:12,685 --> 00:18:14,687
[cutlery clattering]

334
00:18:16,731 --> 00:18:19,317
- [Gosha] Dig in, it's your favorite.
- [Legoshi] Um...

335
00:18:22,028 --> 00:18:24,906
I'm... I'm sorry
I dropped out of school. Is...

336
00:18:24,989 --> 00:18:26,491
Is that why you're here?

337
00:18:26,574 --> 00:18:29,160
[sighs] What's going on with you?

338
00:18:29,244 --> 00:18:32,038
You've got all these huge scars
across your face.

339
00:18:32,122 --> 00:18:34,833
- You ought to be coming to me for advice.
- I don't want to do that.

340
00:18:34,916 --> 00:18:38,920
My mom needed your help before,
and you didn't give it to her, did you?

341
00:18:39,003 --> 00:18:40,004
Now, hold on...

342
00:18:40,088 --> 00:18:43,258
I need you to know that
I am grateful that you raised me,

343
00:18:43,341 --> 00:18:46,219
but from now on,
I want to take care of myself.

344
00:18:46,302 --> 00:18:47,137
[Gosha] Mmm.

345
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,972
[eagle 1] You know what you want?

346
00:18:49,055 --> 00:18:51,474
[eagle 2] Whatever I got last time
was good. What was that?

347
00:18:51,558 --> 00:18:53,309
How should I know? I'm not your mom.

348
00:18:54,269 --> 00:18:57,188
I understand.
You're a grown man after all.

349
00:18:57,272 --> 00:18:59,858
But promise me
you'll remember what I taught you.

350
00:19:00,358 --> 00:19:02,610
Rather, what I would've liked
to teach you.

351
00:19:03,528 --> 00:19:05,238
What I always tried to teach you.

352
00:19:05,321 --> 00:19:07,782
[Legoshi] Be a pacifist. Right?

353
00:19:08,950 --> 00:19:11,452
- I would never forget.
- Hmm.

354
00:19:12,203 --> 00:19:13,163
Good lad.

355
00:19:14,455 --> 00:19:15,540
[both] Hmm?

356
00:19:16,249 --> 00:19:17,292
[eagle 1] Yo.

357
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:21,004
Who let a venomous slug like you
sit in the good seats?

358
00:19:21,087 --> 00:19:22,714
Diner's filling up, old man.

359
00:19:23,256 --> 00:19:27,135
How about we find you a more suitable seat
before you stink up the place?

360
00:19:27,218 --> 00:19:28,928
- Yeah.
- Sorry?

361
00:19:29,429 --> 00:19:31,306
- What? Hmm?
- Huh?

362
00:19:31,389 --> 00:19:32,557
[chair clatters]

363
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:35,518
Legoshi, let's go. Legoshi!

364
00:19:35,602 --> 00:19:37,979
I didn't really understand
what you meant there.

365
00:19:39,063 --> 00:19:42,192
Are you suggesting
Komodo venom is somehow airborne?

366
00:19:42,275 --> 00:19:44,527
- Because that's not true.
- Huh?

367
00:19:45,111 --> 00:19:48,406
You know what he meant, you mutt.
What, do you want to go?

368
00:19:48,489 --> 00:19:50,450
Yeah, I'm happy to take it outside.

369
00:19:50,533 --> 00:19:51,659
Legoshi...

370
00:19:51,743 --> 00:19:53,745
[both snarling]

371
00:19:57,707 --> 00:19:59,709
[owner] I'm only going to say this once.

372
00:20:00,418 --> 00:20:03,254
We expect all of our customers
to follow the rules.

373
00:20:03,338 --> 00:20:05,798
Those who do not
will be kindly asked to leave.

374
00:20:05,882 --> 00:20:06,716
[grunts]

375
00:20:07,508 --> 00:20:10,011
Consider yourself lucky
the owner's a reptile.

376
00:20:10,929 --> 00:20:14,182
- [eagle 1] Let's get out of this place.
- [eagle 2] I didn't wanna eat here anyway.

377
00:20:17,227 --> 00:20:18,728
[owner] Unbelievable.

378
00:20:18,811 --> 00:20:21,689
Excuse me, uh, do you do ant shakes here?

379
00:20:21,773 --> 00:20:23,358
- Best in town.
- Oh, great.

380
00:20:23,441 --> 00:20:25,360
- I'd like a medium, please.
- [Gosha] <i>Legoshi...</i>

381
00:20:25,443 --> 00:20:27,779
<i>- When are you going to learn?</i>
- [owner] Coming right up.

382
00:20:37,163 --> 00:20:38,373
[Gosha] Tell me something.

383
00:20:38,456 --> 00:20:41,334
What part of the word "pacifism"
do you not understand?

384
00:20:41,417 --> 00:20:45,421
That was different. I can't back down
on a situation like that. It's wrong.

385
00:20:45,505 --> 00:20:48,216
I'm not going to sit back and watch
like when I was a child.

386
00:20:48,299 --> 00:20:50,426
Oh, right, because you're so grown up now.

387
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:51,761
[Legoshi sighs]

388
00:20:51,844 --> 00:20:53,846
Look, if you want to survive
in this society,

389
00:20:53,930 --> 00:20:55,890
then get this through your thick skull.

390
00:20:56,516 --> 00:20:59,143
In situations like that,
just let it slide.

391
00:20:59,227 --> 00:21:01,854
You're not going to solve any problems
with fighting!

392
00:21:01,938 --> 00:21:02,981
- [flapping]
- Huh?

393
00:21:03,564 --> 00:21:04,691
Huh? Huh.

394
00:21:05,817 --> 00:21:07,485
[eagles grunt]

395
00:21:08,653 --> 00:21:10,947
- [eagle 1 sneers]
- Huh? [grunts]

396
00:21:11,030 --> 00:21:14,993
Yo. You made me look like an ass
back there, you know that?

397
00:21:15,076 --> 00:21:16,077
[groans softly]

398
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:20,540
Kind of sucks for you that you've wandered
into this secluded alleyway.

399
00:21:20,623 --> 00:21:22,208
Do you know what time it is?

400
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:25,503
- Time for a lesson in etiquette!
- [Legoshi grunts]

401
00:21:25,586 --> 00:21:27,130
- [gasps]
- [Gosha grunts]

402
00:21:27,213 --> 00:21:28,840
- [Gosha growls]
- [eagle 1 gasps]

403
00:21:29,632 --> 00:21:31,759
Keep your mitts off my grandson!

404
00:21:31,843 --> 00:21:33,428
[yells in pain]

405
00:21:34,762 --> 00:21:38,891
[snarls] Those feathers of yours
are so soft and pretty.

406
00:21:38,975 --> 00:21:41,311
You're lucky I haven't sprayed them
with my poison.

407
00:21:41,394 --> 00:21:42,520
Damn you!

408
00:21:42,603 --> 00:21:43,771
[both grunt]

409
00:21:48,192 --> 00:21:51,946
Mmm, you know what they say.
When you've got it, you've got it.

410
00:21:52,739 --> 00:21:53,573
[gasps]

411
00:21:54,824 --> 00:21:55,950
<i>Grandpa...</i>

412
00:21:57,201 --> 00:21:58,494
<i>Who are you?</i>

413
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,999
[special closing theme song playing]
